    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 015.1 — aftermath in the northern mountains"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Northern Mountain Range, Ash Giant Territory"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 10,550, month 1, day 14"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Korrhan, Ash Giant survivors"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: The surviving Ash Giants return to their mountain territory permanently damaged by the broken convergence, assess their inability to survive normally in the mountains, and confront the possibility that isolation may now mean extinction."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Follows the Nephilim purification and incomplete transformation in scene 014.2"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: playable-cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: The Ash Giants' return to their mountain refuge, assessment of their permanent bodily damage, and realization of their vulnerability."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Korrhan's stone-flesh had solidified unevenly—half-molten scars marking where the ritual's heat had exceeded survivable thresholds, creating permanent deformations that would never fully heal."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "Around the Ash Giant leader, the survivors of its tribe bore similar damage."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Forty-three Giants had participated in the convergence."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty-nine remained conscious."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Of those, perhaps fifteen retained enough coherence to contribute meaningfully to tribal survival."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "The Gruulith were gone—purified by Nephilim efficiency that made no distinction between willing servants and programmed slaves."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "The immediate threat had been eliminated."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "But the Ash Giants were broken."
  - line: 40
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We can't survive another season like this,\""
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "one of the tribal elders rumbled, its voice fractured by the same damage that scarred its stone-flesh. \"The ritual's heat destroyed our ability to properly regulate temperature. We're too damaged to endure winter, too fragile to withstand the pressure changes that mountain life requires.\""
  - line: 43
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Korrhan
    text: "\"The other tribes—\""
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Even if those accusations weren't entirely fair—the Gruulith had been purpose-built to exploit Ash Giant territories specifically—they carried enough truth to make requesting aid feel like confirming the other tribes' judgment."
  - line: 47
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We could migrate,\""
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "another survivor suggested. \"Descend to lower altitudes where temperature regulation isn't as critical—\""
  - line: 50
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And enter Forest Giant territory? Desert lands? They barely tolerate our presence at inter-tribal gatherings. They won't welcome refugees who represent everything they blamed for the ritual's cost.\""
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "The mathematics were brutal."
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "The Ash Giants needed resources they couldn't produce, healing they couldn't achieve, integration with tribes who viewed them as liability rather than ally."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "They could attempt proud isolation—maintain their damaged territories, slowly die across generations as their fragmented bodies proved insufficient for survival."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Or they could accept alternative arrangements."
  - line: 58
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "Year 10,550, Month 1, Day 17"

